<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arizpe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arizpe is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sonora">Sonora</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, on the Sonora River, founded as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> mission in 1646. In 1776 it was made the seat of the Commandancy General of the Internal Provinces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teodoro-de-croix">Teodoro de Croix</a>, briefly serving as the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s northern frontier. The explorer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-bautista-de-anza">Juan Bautista de Anza</a> is buried in its church.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arizpe.jpg" alt="Arizpe" width="320" height="290" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LIMO 5 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iglesia_de_nuestra_se%C3%B1ora_de_la_asunci%C3%B3n,_arizpe,_sonora.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
